/-!
# The explicit Sylow subgroup of the HS permutation normalizer

The ten generator squares and 45 inverse-conjugation identities satisfy the
triangular binary-collection criterion. Thus the 1024 ascending binary products
cover the generated subgroup. A checked decoder recovers the binary index
from the images of letters 0, 1 and 2, proving the products distinct and the
subgroup order exactly 1024.

The generic collection theorem is in `Theory.GroupTheory.BinaryCollection`.
Finite identities and decoder equations are checked by kernel reduction.
Source context: Aschbacher–Smith 16.1.5(10), p.1172; GLS3 Table 5.3m.
Fixed witness data and their GAP discovery script are retained in `source/`.
-/

